<i>Two-Mike-Mike-Whiskey-Delta.</i>

1064
01:19:02,732 --> 01:19:04,035
<i>Do you copy?</i>

1065
01:19:07,737 --> 01:19:08,771
[radio static]

1066
01:19:08,806 --> 01:19:10,008
[radio operator]<i> Grand Jun--</i>

1067
01:19:14,576 --> 01:19:18,184
Grand Junction, this is Cessna
Two-Mike-Mike-Whiskey-Delta.

1068
01:19:18,219 --> 01:19:19,685
Do you copy?

1069
01:19:19,720 --> 01:19:20,752
[radio operator]
<i>Grand Junction...</i>

1070
01:19:20,787 --> 01:19:23,989
<i>Is anyone...</i>
<i>Repeat. Grand Jun--</i>

1071
01:19:24,888 --> 01:19:26,187
Grand Junction, do you copy?

1072
01:19:26,222 --> 01:19:28,821
This is Cessna
Two-Mike-Mike-Whiskey-Delta.

1073
01:19:28,856 --> 01:19:31,227
Do you copy?

1074
01:19:31,262 --> 01:19:34,197
[radio operator]<i> Copy that,</i>
<i>Cessna. Are you real?</i>

1075
01:19:35,634 --> 01:19:37,065
Yeah. [chuckles] Yeah.

1076
01:19:37,101 --> 01:19:38,465
[radio operator]
<i>Well, I'll be damned.</i>

1077
01:19:38,500 --> 01:19:41,139
<i>It's been two years</i>
<i>since an aircraft responded.</i>

1078
01:19:41,174 --> 01:19:43,704
<i>I didn't think there were</i>
<i>any more of you up there.</i>

1079
01:19:43,740 --> 01:19:45,107
Uh, likewise.

1080
01:19:45,143 --> 01:19:47,578
Uh, we're out of Erie.
Just-- Just near Denver.

1081
01:19:47,613 --> 01:19:48,812
We've come a long ways.

1082
01:19:48,848 --> 01:19:50,745
We were thinking
we might stop by.

1083
01:19:50,781 --> 01:19:52,119
There's three of us.

1084
01:19:52,155 --> 01:19:53,348
[radio static]

1085
01:19:55,921 --> 01:19:57,185
[radio operator]
<i>No offense, Cessna,</i>

1086
01:19:57,220 --> 01:19:59,624
<i>I... I appreciate</i>
<i>the conversation,</i>

1087
01:19:59,659 --> 01:20:02,124
<i>but we'd prefer you move along.</i>

1088
01:20:02,159 --> 01:20:04,898
<i>We haven't been lucky</i>
<i>with visitors.</i>

1089
01:20:05,929 --> 01:20:07,895
We won't cause any trouble.

1090
01:20:07,930 --> 01:20:09,298
We don't mean any harm.

1091
01:20:10,232 --> 01:20:11,801
[radio operator]
<i>Well, no offense,</i>

1092
01:20:11,836 --> 01:20:14,303
<i>but who would say different?</i>

1093
01:20:16,343 --> 01:20:17,306
Understood.

1094
01:20:17,840 --> 01:20:19,010
[Pops stutters]

1095
01:20:19,145 --> 01:20:22,946
There used to be a hell of
a pancake store downtown.

1096
01:20:22,981 --> 01:20:25,213
Um, Sandy's
I think it was called.

1097
01:20:25,249 --> 01:20:27,654
Uh, I was a little partial to
the blueberry.

1098
01:20:27,690 --> 01:20:29,489
She used to sprinkle
something on top.

1099
01:20:29,524 --> 01:20:30,820
I can't remember what it was.

1100
01:20:30,856 --> 01:20:33,786
It was--
It was fantastic. Um...

1101
01:20:33,821 --> 01:20:36,726
[radio operator]<i> Sandy would</i>
<i>chop up marshmallows real fine</i>

1102
01:20:36,761 --> 01:20:39,226
<i>and then shake 'em over.</i>

1103
01:20:39,261 --> 01:20:43,530
Yeah. Yeah.
That's it. Best ever.

1104
01:20:46,105 --> 01:20:47,906
[radio operator]
<i>Keep your approach, Cessna.</i>

1105
01:20:47,941 --> 01:20:49,440
<i>We'll see you folks</i>
<i>when you get here.</i>

1106
01:20:49,476 --> 01:20:50,339
[radio beeps]

1107
01:20:53,814 --> 01:20:55,042
-[Pops] You're welcome.
-[chuckles]

1108
01:20:55,077 --> 01:20:57,544
Copy you. We'll see you soon.

1109
01:20:58,947 --> 01:21:01,284
[Hig, Cima laugh]

1110
01:21:06,727 --> 01:21:08,929
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1111
01:21:30,548 --> 01:21:33,183
[Hig on radio]<i> Grand Junction,</i>
<i>this is Two-Whiskey-Delta.</i>

1112
01:21:33,218 --> 01:21:36,484
<i>Southeast at 3,000 feet</i>
<i>inbound for landing.</i>

1113
01:21:37,924 --> 01:21:39,255
[radio operator]
<i>I see you, Cessna.</i>

1114
01:21:39,291 --> 01:21:41,921
<i>Two-Whiskey-Delta make</i>
<i>a straight in approach,</i>

1115
01:21:41,956 --> 01:21:43,122
<i>runway 22.</i>

1116
01:21:43,157 --> 01:21:44,794
<i>You're clear to land.</i>

1117
01:21:44,830 --> 01:21:46,934
Copy that, Grand Junction.

1118
01:21:46,969 --> 01:21:49,836
[radio operator]<i> Welcome to</i>
<i>Grand Junction, Cessna.</i>

1119
01:21:49,872 --> 01:21:51,597
<i>Couple of our folks</i>
<i>are gonna meet you.</i>

1120
01:21:51,632 --> 01:21:54,268
<i>And no weapons please,</i>
<i>if you're carrying.</i>

1121
01:21:54,303 --> 01:21:57,403
<i>It's the only real rule</i>
<i>we've got.</i>

1122
01:21:57,438 --> 01:21:59,307
[Hig] All due respect,
you're as, uh--

1123
01:21:59,342 --> 01:22:01,911
you're as unknown to us
as we are to you.

1124
01:22:01,946 --> 01:22:03,047
[radio operator]<i> Understood.</i>

1125
01:22:03,249 --> 01:22:05,618
<i>And you are free to keep</i>
<i>flying the friendly skies</i>

1126
01:22:05,653 --> 01:22:07,053
<i>if you're not comfortable.</i>

1127
01:22:07,587 --> 01:22:08,615
What do we think?

1128
01:22:09,258 --> 01:22:10,857
Exposes us.

1129
01:22:10,893 --> 01:22:14,692
Yeah. I guess it depends
how much we trust 'em.

1130
01:22:14,727 --> 01:22:16,194
We trust 'em a little.

1131
01:22:17,662 --> 01:22:18,933
Thanks, man.

1132
01:22:22,770 --> 01:22:24,939
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

1133
01:22:37,783 --> 01:22:39,987
[propeller whirring]

1134
01:22:58,874 --> 01:23:00,601
What are we doing
in this piece of shit?

1135
01:23:13,686 --> 01:23:15,682
[♪ music fades]

1136
01:23:27,062 --> 01:23:28,497
[Pops groans]

1137
01:23:33,475 --> 01:23:34,734
[keys jingle]

1138
01:23:38,007 --> 01:23:39,911
How are you doing?

1139
01:23:39,947 --> 01:23:43,182
Welcome. I'm John.
This is Logan.

1140
01:23:44,419 --> 01:23:46,982
Hi. I'm Hig.

1141
01:23:47,018 --> 01:23:50,020
And this is Pops and Cima.

1142
01:23:50,056 --> 01:23:51,951
Any illnesses
we should know of?

1143
01:23:51,987 --> 01:23:53,727
I'm sorry.

1144
01:23:53,763 --> 01:23:55,991
Logan likes to
get to the point.

1145
01:23:56,026 --> 01:23:59,099
No. No, no illnesses.

1146
01:23:59,833 --> 01:24:01,596
Well, if you wouldn't mind.

1147
01:24:10,073 --> 01:24:10,971
[thermometer beeps]

1148
01:24:11,007 --> 01:24:12,574
That's a green.

1149
01:24:16,846 --> 01:24:18,218
[beeps]

1150
01:24:18,254 --> 01:24:19,515
Yep.

1151
01:24:21,752 --> 01:24:22,481
[beeps]

1152
01:24:22,517 --> 01:24:25,488
[John] Ah, beautiful.
Thank you.

1153
01:24:26,923 --> 01:24:28,227
Follow me.

1154
01:24:29,829 --> 01:24:31,124
You get to meet Darlene.

1155
01:24:31,160 --> 01:24:32,762
[Pops clears throat]

1156
01:24:32,798 --> 01:24:34,497
[owl hooting]

1157
01:24:38,299 --> 01:24:40,435
Through here, Pops.

1158
01:24:40,470 --> 01:24:42,269
Been a while
since I've seen one of these.

1159
01:24:42,304 --> 01:24:43,402
-Just a precaution.
-[beeps]

1160
01:24:43,438 --> 01:24:45,576
[♪ classical music playing]

1161
01:24:45,611 --> 01:24:46,608
[beeps]

1162
01:24:49,351 --> 01:24:50,843
[buzzes]

1163
01:24:54,019 --> 01:24:56,282
<i>I don't blame you, Cessna.</i>

1164
01:24:56,317 --> 01:24:57,855
<i>It's understandable.</i>

1165
01:24:57,890 --> 01:25:00,226
<i>New place, new faces.</i>

1166
01:25:00,261 --> 01:25:04,565
<i>Takes a lot of faith,</i>
<i>especially in this world.</i>

1167
01:25:04,600 --> 01:25:07,131
<i>But rules are rules.</i>

1168
01:25:07,166 --> 01:25:10,335
We'll get it back to you.
Follow me.

1169
01:25:12,500 --> 01:25:14,702
[♪ classical music continues]

1170
01:25:19,981 --> 01:25:21,513
[people chattering
indistinctly]

1171
01:25:21,548 --> 01:25:24,083
[♪ music playing, Dean Martin
"Memories Are Made Of This"]

1172
01:25:24,118 --> 01:25:27,352
♪<i> Take one fresh</i>
<i>And tender kiss</i> ♪

1173
01:25:27,388 --> 01:25:29,990
♪<i> You can't beat</i>
<i>The memories you've given me</i> ♪

1174
01:25:30,025 --> 01:25:33,953
♪<i> Add one stolen night</i>
<i>Of bliss</i> ♪

1175
01:25:33,989 --> 01:25:36,256
♪<i> You can't beat the memories</i>
<i>You've given me...</i> ♪

1176
01:25:36,292 --> 01:25:38,358
A welcome for our guests.

1177
01:25:38,393 --> 01:25:40,563
[people applauding, cheering]

1178
01:25:45,105 --> 01:25:47,306
-[person whistles]
-[applauding]

1179
01:25:47,873 --> 01:25:49,308
Hmm. Let's go.

1180
01:25:50,878 --> 01:25:51,945
Better not keep her waiting.

1181
01:25:52,047 --> 01:25:55,611
♪<i> Don't forget</i>
<i>A small moonbeam</i> ♪

1182
01:25:55,647 --> 01:25:58,212
♪<i> You can't beat</i>
<i>The memories you've given me</i> ♪

1183
01:25:58,247 --> 01:25:59,315
[no audible dialogue]

1184
01:25:59,417 --> 01:26:02,783
♪<i> Fold it lightly</i>
<i>With a dream</i> ♪

1185
01:26:02,819 --> 01:26:06,258
♪<i> You can't beat</i>
<i>The memories you've given me</i> ♪

1186
01:26:06,294 --> 01:26:13,164
♪<i> Your lips and mine</i>
<i>Two sips of wine</i> ♪

1187
01:26:13,199 --> 01:26:17,167
♪<i> Memories are made of this</i> ♪

1188
01:26:17,203 --> 01:26:19,272
[people chattering
indistinctly]

1189
01:26:20,073 --> 01:26:22,238
[♪ classical music playing]

1190
01:26:22,273 --> 01:26:25,674
-Welcome.
-Please. Be seated.

1191
01:26:28,144 --> 01:26:29,174
[door closes]

1192
01:26:29,210 --> 01:26:30,481
All right.

1193
01:26:36,151 --> 01:26:37,185
[exclaims]

1194
01:26:37,220 --> 01:26:39,655
There you are, Cessna.

1195
01:26:40,154 --> 01:26:41,726
Oh.

1196
01:26:41,762 --> 01:26:43,624
In the flesh.

1197
01:26:43,659 --> 01:26:45,892
Do you mind? I wanna
commemorate this moment.

1198
01:26:46,767 --> 01:26:47,861
Say "cheese."

1199
01:26:50,331 --> 01:26:51,863
[exhales deeply]

1200
01:26:51,899 --> 01:26:55,242
And a fine looking
little trio to boot. Hmm.

1201
01:26:55,710 --> 01:26:59,272
Hig, Cima, Pops.

1202
01:26:59,308 --> 01:27:01,377
It's Jack, actually.

1203
01:27:01,412 --> 01:27:04,480
Hig there is the pilot.
This is Darlene.

1204
01:27:04,515 --> 01:27:07,985
Darlene, thank you
for letting us drop in.

1205
01:27:08,021 --> 01:27:09,487
Tell me about your story.

1206
01:27:09,522 --> 01:27:12,520
Now, I don't get to talk
to new faces very often, so...

1207
01:27:12,555 --> 01:27:14,093
Now, Jack,
I heard you used to spend

1208
01:27:14,129 --> 01:27:16,330
some time with Sandy
and her pancakes?

1209
01:27:17,399 --> 01:27:20,396
Well, uh, me and my old man
used to buy a lot of livestock

1210
01:27:20,431 --> 01:27:22,101
at the auctions here
back in the day.

1211
01:27:22,136 --> 01:27:23,795
So, I'd end up
with one of Sandy's

1212
01:27:23,831 --> 01:27:26,337
blueberry pancakes
as a... as a treat.

1213
01:27:26,372 --> 01:27:28,875
Perfect little town
back in those days.

1214
01:27:28,911 --> 01:27:30,138
-[Pops chuckles]
-Trying our best

1215
01:27:30,174 --> 01:27:31,443
to build one again.

1216
01:27:32,675 --> 01:27:35,578
[singing]
♪<i> Fly me to the moon</i> ♪

1217
01:27:35,613 --> 01:27:39,052
♪<i> And let me play</i>
<i>Among the stars</i> ♪

1218
01:27:39,088 --> 01:27:41,181
Once a stewardess,
always a stewardess.

1219
01:27:41,217 --> 01:27:42,487
[Hig] Thank you.

1220
01:27:45,660 --> 01:27:46,857
Drink up.

1221
01:27:46,892 --> 01:27:47,961
[Pops sighs]

1222
01:27:47,996 --> 01:27:49,792
-Thank you.
-[Darlene] Mm-hmm.

1223
01:27:49,828 --> 01:27:53,894
[whispers] So, darling, do you
ever speak or are you just...

1224
01:27:54,736 --> 01:27:56,336
window dressing?

1225
01:27:57,167 --> 01:27:59,337
Occasionally.

1226
01:27:59,373 --> 01:28:02,276
And what do you think
of our little spot here?

1227
01:28:03,943 --> 01:28:05,938
It's interesting.

1228
01:28:05,974 --> 01:28:08,447
Almost like you flew
through a time warp, right?

1229
01:28:09,015 --> 01:28:10,777
Drink up. There's more.

1230
01:28:10,813 --> 01:28:12,750
Now I've got something
stronger if you'd like.

1231
01:28:12,786 --> 01:28:13,612
[stutters]

1232
01:28:13,647 --> 01:28:15,086
I wouldn't say no to something

1233
01:28:15,121 --> 01:28:16,517
with a little more kick to it.

1234
01:28:16,553 --> 01:28:19,018
How about
160 proof worth, Jack?

1235
01:28:20,060 --> 01:28:22,822
Just like my grandpa taught me.

1236
01:28:22,857 --> 01:28:25,057
-This ain't no vodka or gin.
-[Pops] Mm-hmm.

1237
01:28:26,068 --> 01:28:28,060
Yeah, tell me
how you like that.

1238
01:28:28,869 --> 01:28:30,103
There you go.

1239
01:28:30,138 --> 01:28:31,766
Well, now,
you haven't touched yours.

1240
01:28:31,802 --> 01:28:34,072
-I'm good. Thanks.
-I'll just give you a topper.

1241
01:28:34,108 --> 01:28:35,472
-Ooh, yeah. That's...
-Right?

1242
01:28:35,507 --> 01:28:37,440
Yeah. That's the kick
I'm talking about.

1243
01:28:37,476 --> 01:28:39,044
I told you.
If we're gonna start over,

1244
01:28:39,079 --> 01:28:40,412
we might as well do it right.

1245
01:28:40,448 --> 01:28:42,912
No fancy cocktails with
umbrellas and fruit and...

1246
01:28:42,947 --> 01:28:44,346
Go on.

1247
01:28:44,381 --> 01:28:46,614
So, tell me about your trip.

1248
01:28:46,650 --> 01:28:49,552
You spot much life
between Erie and us?

1249
01:28:49,588 --> 01:28:51,791
I mean, there's a few pockets
here and there.

1250
01:28:51,827 --> 01:28:52,617
But nothing nearby.

1251
01:28:52,653 --> 01:28:54,760
[♪ tense music playing]

1252
01:28:54,796 --> 01:28:55,890
Good to know.

1253
01:28:57,627 --> 01:28:59,127
Have you had
a lot of trouble here?

1254
01:28:59,162 --> 01:29:00,327
Oh. [scoffs]

1255
01:29:00,363 --> 01:29:01,597
Book of Psalms 121,

1256
01:29:01,632 --> 01:29:03,500
"The Lord will
protect people from all evil

1257
01:29:03,536 --> 01:29:05,467
and guard them as they
go about their lives."

1258
01:29:05,503 --> 01:29:07,435
-Praise God.
-[John, Logan] Amen.

1259
01:29:07,470 --> 01:29:09,042
This is where he's been hiding

1260
01:29:09,078 --> 01:29:10,872
for the last few years.
[chuckles]

1261
01:29:13,014 --> 01:29:14,777
[Pops continues chuckling]

1262
01:29:17,345 --> 01:29:18,479
So, Jack...

1263
01:29:18,514 --> 01:29:20,651
[♪ tense music continues]

1264
01:29:25,656 --> 01:29:27,754
You and Big Hig,
your hands always this rough

1265
01:29:27,789 --> 01:29:30,529
before the world
turned upside down?

1266
01:29:30,564 --> 01:29:34,566
Uh, well, I've been a rancher
all my life, so yeah.

1267
01:29:36,035 --> 01:29:37,068
What about you?

1268
01:29:37,104 --> 01:29:39,537
I was a mechanic, mostly.

1269
01:29:39,573 --> 01:29:42,170
Darlene, you mind if I, uh--
you mind if I smoke?

1270
01:29:42,205 --> 01:29:43,575
Smoke it up.

1271
01:29:45,676 --> 01:29:48,514
Solid, hardworking laborers.
I respect that.

1272
01:29:49,816 --> 01:29:50,846
And you?

1273
01:29:52,051 --> 01:29:53,420
Medical resident.

1274
01:29:53,986 --> 01:29:56,448
My, oh, my.

1275
01:29:56,484 --> 01:29:59,258
John, a doctor.

1276
01:29:59,293 --> 01:30:01,024
We don't have
one of those around.

1277
01:30:01,060 --> 01:30:02,429
No, we haven't.

1278
01:30:03,195 --> 01:30:04,562
You should've told me

1279
01:30:04,598 --> 01:30:07,459
what valuable cargo
you were carrying, Big Hig.

1280
01:30:07,495 --> 01:30:09,035
I had no idea.

1281
01:30:09,070 --> 01:30:11,402
You see, laborers like you two,

1282
01:30:11,437 --> 01:30:14,636
they eat the same amount
as the rest,

1283
01:30:14,671 --> 01:30:16,437
and we've already got
more than enough

1284
01:30:16,472 --> 01:30:17,574
for that kind of work.

1285
01:30:17,743 --> 01:30:20,245
But now a real-life doctor,
that is worth a share.

1286
01:30:20,281 --> 01:30:21,344
[stutters]
Ah, you got me wrong.

1287
01:30:21,379 --> 01:30:22,948
I'm actually not a real doctor.

1288
01:30:22,984 --> 01:30:24,416
I was just studying,

1289
01:30:24,452 --> 01:30:26,045
and I honestly barely
remember anything, so...

1290
01:30:26,081 --> 01:30:29,219
Oh, I'm sure it's like
ridin' a bike. [chuckles]

1291
01:30:29,254 --> 01:30:30,721
[chuckles] Yes, ma'am.

1292
01:30:31,222 --> 01:30:32,886
[Darlene gasps]

1293
01:30:32,921 --> 01:30:36,463
Logan, how'd you like
to marry a doctor?

1294
01:30:37,393 --> 01:30:38,460
What the fuck?

1295
01:30:38,495 --> 01:30:40,130
Oh, I'd like that, Darlene.

1296
01:30:40,165 --> 01:30:41,930
I'd like that too.

1297
01:30:43,637 --> 01:30:45,868
I think maybe the time
for our conversation is over.

1298
01:30:45,903 --> 01:30:47,867
-Don't be rude, Jack.
-It's, uh, time for us to go.

1299
01:30:47,902 --> 01:30:49,806
-[Darlene] Jack. Jack.
-Not being rude.

1300
